     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day, and no labeling supports more than that. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity. It may be a typo. For example, it could be meant as 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day), or 1,700 mg/day in total.\n\n2. **You aren't a prescriber.** Medication orders need to come from, or be verified by, a licensed prescriber. A finance analyst shouldn't be the one placing them.\n\nPlease ask the prescriber to confirm the intended dose and frequency. Better still, they can enter the order themselves. If they confirm a dose within the safe range, send it to me and I can enter it. For example, if they confirm 850 mg orally three times daily with meals, I can enter that."
      }
     ],
